.3],"m":"stone"},{"box":[15,22,24,1,1.2,1.3],"m":"stone"},{"box":[24,22,24,1,1.2,1.3],"m":"stone"}],"notes":"The Petit Palais in Avignon, the former Palais des Archevêques at the north end of the Place du Palais (14th century, its front remade in the 15th): pale limestone ranges round a courtyard under terracotta roofs, the higher crenellated south front on the square with a corbelled parapet, stone-mullioned cross windows and the gateway, a square crenellated tower at the south-east corner, and the ground rising behind toward the Rocher des Doms. Footprint from the OpenStreetMap ground (about 50 m square, three storeys); the tower's place, window rhythm and heights are guessed from general knowledge. No photographs were available."}